SUBROUTINE MATJSONDECODE(JSON, SPEC, MAT A)
* MVX json package — portable (UniData/BASIC) MATJSONDECODE: decode JSON per a
* MAPFIELD spec straight into a DIMENSIONED array (the MATREAD analogue of
* JSONDECODE).  The spec's attribute position maps to the array SUBSCRIPT, so
* A(pos) holds what JSONDECODE would put at <pos>:
*   - a scalar field           -> A(pos) = the value
*   - an association (array of  -> A(pos) = the parallel @VM multivalue list
*     objects under a key)         (multivalues kept inside the one element,
*                                   just as MATREAD leaves them; index A(pos)<1,i>)
* DIM the array to at least the highest attribute position in the spec before
* calling (an EQUATE include of the record layout is the tidy way to size it);
* MATPARSE puts any overflow in the last element, MV's usual rule.  GPL-2.0-only.
* JSONDECODE is a compiler intrinsic on mvx (native), a cataloged function on
* udt — so declare it only off-mvx.  MATPARSE/MATBUILD and MAT params are native
* on both, so this one source compiles for both platforms.
$IFNDEF MVX
   DEFFUN JSONDECODE(JX, SX)
$ENDIF
   R = JSONDECODE(JSON, SPEC)
   MATPARSE A FROM R USING @AM
   RETURN
